# Project roadmap

This document tracks the phased milestones for Rocci and Rocdown.

## Milestones

### Phase 1: Project-shell seam & named layouts (Completed)
- Configurable `theme` in `rocdown.toml`.
- Project-local `.rocci` theme compilation into modules.
- Named layout validation and view record expansion.

### Phase 2: Complete rocci.dev structure (Current)
- Canonical route tree under `site/`.
- Branded shell and named layout templates in `.rocci`.
- Route aliases preserving backwards compatibility.
- Structural pages across Home, Rocdown, Docs, News, FAQ, and Project portals.

### Phase 3: Typed collections & feeds
- First-class collection definitions in Rocdown.
- Automated `news` catalog queries and Atom / RSS feed generation.
- Recent-news integration into Home and Section views.

### Phase 4: Extended capabilities
- Static client-side search indexing with zero runtime dependencies.
- Reusable site starter templates and distribution packaging.
